{"agent":"bg81","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The reducer no longer applies an event's `evidence` field at all, so a `bug invalid` closure whose probe is stored as `evidence` (the split described on `Bug.found_evidence`) never lands on the record. Replaying or folding `{subject: bug id, data: {evidence: \"probe showed false\"}}` leaves `bug.evidence == \"\"`. The same line also drops historical `bug found` events that only have `evidence`, not `found_evidence`: a state rebuild loses the text that previously populated `bug.evidence`, with no fallback read of `ev.data[\"evidence\"]`.","digest":"b16b37008b4fea8c","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/core/handlers/knowledge.py:102","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/handlers/knowledge.py:102"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Renaming the stored key to `found_evidence` does not stop the agent-supplied command from running. The bug is that MCP `evidence` is passed as `repro_cmd` and executed by the shell (`surfaces/declared/records.py` / `services/reprobundle.py`); those paths are not in this change, help text is unchanged, and there is no digest gate or sandbox. An MCP `evidence` value such as `touch /tmp/marker && echo $HOST_SECRET` is still handed to the shell with the host environment; the regression assertion only checks the renamed field after the fact and does not fail that execution.","digest":"030e7a9199de2a97","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:104","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:104"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":2,"delta_from":"174eb1e674a733c1ea4faf02be4c916f7530adf1","delta_raised":["b16b37008b4fea8c","030e7a9199de2a97"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":3247,"diff_sha":"73044197d2daf4d06cd89a22660ba94665bba9bea573962fd87a6646cab56599","diff_source":"delta review of 2 commits since 174eb1e674","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"unt