{"agent":"bg81","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The reducer no longer applies an event's `evidence` field at all, so a `bug invalid` closure whose probe is stored as `evidence` (the split described on `Bug.found_evidence`) never lands on the record. Replaying or folding `{subject: bug id, data: {evidence: \"probe showed false\"}}` leaves `bug.evidence == \"\"`. The same line also drops historical `bug found` events that only have `evidence`, not `found_evidence`: a state rebuild loses the text that previously populated `bug.evidence`, with no fallback read of `ev.data[\"evidence\"]`.","digest":"b16b37008b4fea8c","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/core/handlers/knowledge.py:102","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/core/handlers/knowledge.py:102"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"Renaming the stored key to `found_evidence` does not stop the agent-supplied command from running. The bug is that MCP `evidence` is passed as `repro_cmd` and executed by the shell (`surfaces/declared/records.py` / `services/reprobundle.py`); those paths are not in this change, help text is unchanged, and there is no digest gate or sandbox. An MCP `evidence` value such as `touch /tmp/marker && echo $HOST_SECRET` is still handed to the shell with the host environment; the regression assertion only checks the renamed field after the fact and does not fail that execution.","digest":"030e7a9199de2a97","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:104","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py:104"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":2,"delta_from":"174eb1e674a733c1ea4faf02be4c916f7530adf1","delta_raised":["b16b37008b4fea8c","030e7a9199de2a97"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":3247,"diff_sha":"73044197d2daf4d06cd89a22660ba94665bba9bea573962fd87a6646cab56599","diff_source":"delta review of 2 commits since 174eb1e674","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":47.6,"family":"xai","findings":2,"full_coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"d6339f406c040c55","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B18cd856a67.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261108T170938Z-379d600a.jsonl","passed_on_refutation":{"confirmed":0,"max_rounds":6,"refutations":[{"digest":"b16b37008b4fea8c","finding":1,"probe":"bug.invalid evidence is folded by _h_bug_invalid (knowledge.py ~190 bug.evidence = ev.data.get('evidence','')), which this change never touches; _h_bug_found never folded 'evidence' for bug.found before (bug.found never wrote 'evidence'), so nothing historical is dropped -- found_evidence is a NEW field. Verified tests/test_bug_invalid.py still passes (19 passed)."},{"digest":"030e7a9199de2a97","finding":2,"probe":"The records.py decoupling (MCP evidence param -> bug_found evidence=, no longer repro_cmd=) IS the core of commit 174eb1e67, reviewed clean in the first (full) round with 0 findings; this delta reviewer only saw the found_evidence rename (2 later commits) and never saw records.py. Empirically the regression test tests/test_repro_verify.py::test_mcp_evidence_is_stored_verbatim_never_executed passes (marker evidence_ran NOT created), failing on unfixed code."}],"refuted":2,"rounds":2},"reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"0915d7ce77af923181e56b5603689a5356471bac","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py":"100644 2bdede0b1285d05e7e68aa01fd9c901dd4e93b15","ddflow/core/handlers/knowledge.py":"100644 bfc78621a58a45f58b1fff198102c55a8366fe81","ddflow/core/records/content.py":"100644 375147630d16697591df51f5bcc9168ee80542fd","ddflow/services/reprocheck.py":"100644 9717c8778ab3b8e840220363db908df294d3b43f","ddflow/surfaces/declared/records.py":"100644 f8057c8261633499b29ef2ba70b1cb7240726ff0","tests/golden/__snapshots__/test_golden_cli_help.ambr":"100644 e103a4d56d4cf2bc66b61b9ef193a924e608dd8d","tests/test_repro_verify.py":"100644 39ff091